# ============================================================================
# SkillForge AI - frontend (public repository)
#
# This repository contains the browser application ONLY. There is no backend
# here and no database credential of any kind - the app talks to a private REST
# API over HTTPS, configured with one variable: VITE_API_BASE_URL.
#
# That split is deliberate. Anything readable by a browser is readable by
# everyone, so nothing secret can live in here even accidentally. The rules
# below exist to keep that true.
# ============================================================================

# --- secrets ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nothing secret should ever reach this repo. These rules are the backstop for
# the day someone pastes a key into a source file "just to test".
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets.json
.credentials

# --- dependencies -------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
.yarn/

# --- build output -------------------------------------------------------------
dist/
build/
.vite/
.vercel/

# --- logs ---------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# --- editor / OS --------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- transient test artifacts --------------------------------------------------
.tmp-*
*.tmp

# --- local AI/editor tooling --------------------------------------------------
# Agent skills, editor hooks and personal config answers. These describe how
# the project is worked on, not what the project is, and they differ per
# machine. Committing them helps nobody and leaks local answers into history.
.agents/
.codex/
.impeccable/
.claude/
.cursor/

# --- IMPORTANT -----------------------------------------------------------------
# vercel.json must stay tracked. It carries the build command, the SPA rewrite
# and every security header, including the Content-Security-Policy. Losing it
# silently removes those headers from the deployed site.
!frontend/vercel.json